I'm using React + typescript, tailwind. How to center the image horizontally?

const Home = () => {
    return (
        <>
            <div className="w-screen">
                <img className="mx-auto" src="https://picsum.photos/400" alt="My Photo" />
            </div>
            <h1 className="text-center">Welcome to My Personal Website</h1>
        </>
    );
}

export default Home;

Your current code is already centering the image horizontally using Tailwind CSS. The `mx-auto` class that you have added to the `<img>` element is responsible for centering the image by applying an equal amount of margin on both the left and right sides.

Here's your `Home` component with minor syntax adjustments:

```javascript
import React from 'react';

const Home = () => {
  return (
    <>
      <div className="w-screen">
        <img
          className="mx-auto"
          src="https://picsum.photos/400"
          alt="My Photo"
        />
      </div>
      <h1 className="text-center">Welcome to My Personal Website</h1>
    </>
  );
};

export default Home;
```

This code should work as intended, and the image should be centered horizontally within the screen.
